1.2.evidence:
CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 5
Every Woman and Child victim of violence has the right:
a. to have their dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. to obtain protection from family, community, Regional Government and other parties either temporarily or based on the determination of a Protection order from the Court;
c. to obtain recovery of physical, psychological and sexual health services in accordance with the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
d. to obtain special handling related to the confidentiality of victims;
e. to obtain assistance by companions and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
f. to obtain spiritual guidance services.

