3.6.evidence:
Article 11
(1) SPM as referred to in Article 9 paragraph (3) has performance indicators comprising:
a. coverage of Women and Children victims of violence who receive complaint handling by trained officers within the UPTD PPA;
b. coverage of Women and Children victims of violence who receive health services by trained health workers at Puskesmas and at Hospitals;
c. coverage of social rehabilitation services provided by trained social rehabilitation officers for Women and Children victims of violence within the UPTD PPA;
d. coverage of spiritual guidance services provided by trained spiritual guidance officers for Women and Children victims of violence within the UPTD PPA;
e. coverage of legal aid services for women and children victims of violence;
f. coverage of recovery services/psychological services for women and children victims of violence;
g. coverage of mediation services for women and children victims of violence;
h. coverage of repatriation services for women and children victims of violence; and
i. coverage of social reintegration services for women and children victims of violence.
(2) The determination of SPM performance indicators of UPTD PPA for Women and Children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) constitutes the minimum target that must be achieved.

